{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793022787,"nonce":"zZATqc5pQi8qW5TX6mDGQqKBvec=","message":"Implemented in fe177b3 (Bound shared document admission).\n\ndoc.open now requires an existing UTF-8 file and applies the existing 8 MiB read limit before materialization, with a post-read check for growth. Missing paths, oversized files, directories and invalid UTF-8 fail before recovery state is written. Creation remains explicit through fs.write. Existing-file baseline state is still persisted before returning it, preserving CRDT recovery consistency.\n\nServer-side admission caps each connection at 256 distinct subscriptions and the workspace at 512 distinct retained documents. Repeated opens do not consume another slot, and another client can share an existing document at the workspace limit. Workspace admission shares the existing opening/release gate, so competing opens cannot both consume the final slot. Only an attached connection can submit doc.update. Explicit close releases subscriptions immediately; disconnections retain the existing five-second reload grace, then idle documents are flushed and evicted. Failed flushes retain recovery rather than dropping dirty state.\n\nValidation: all 38 native tests passed, including four new real-socket tests. They cover signed and unsigned missing-path probes without files/state; explicit file creation followed by open; size/binary/directory refusals; at least 65 code tabs (the test fills all 256 connection slots); duplicate subscriptions; overflow rejection without state; racing opens for the final workspace slot; sharing while full; unsubscribe/close/disconnect capacity recovery; and unattached update rejection. Core-only cargo check passed. All 37 browser-session tests passed against the rebuilt native binary. Two full WASM editors passed edit/undo/Save/reconnect/reload, tab lifecycle, replacement-state fencing, actual toast reopen and original-draft preservation without a runtime error.\n\nRebuilt WASM and native session, staged the tested bundle at bin/web/rayde, and restarted the local service at 127.0.0.1:7070 with workspace/URL/credentials/environment preserved. A read-only live probe verified that doc.open of an unknown path is rejected and leaves no file, while normal workspace access still works. Served browser adapter hash matches the tested bundle. WASM 6bd50e26d6c630fa113e6119418ad2a7afd6b4e1059c8865d3e6e0201d5b7d45; adapter 51df1406f7e3ad6bdf098d183883602c3116659358d8b5cda48aa25f52b2ac79. No push or deployment.\n\nThis completes document-admission controls only. It is not an aggregate RAM/byte/rate/storage quota or a fix for all browser heap use. Per-identity connection limits, durable DO document authority, MSB provisioning and broader resource accounting remain open in their parent tracks.","files":null}]}